  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As a world creator, the best data I can gather outside of the editor is from real-world data from the users' experience. Everyone has a unique experience of running on vastly different hardware and computers. I have a heavy focus on world optimization for a variety of different worlds; whether that be hangout spaces, DJ venues, or games and experiences. \nBeing able to see, at a glance, the average framerate for each individual user in an instance gives me the feedback I need to produce better content for everyone on all platforms. I'm sure this is possible with Udon# but I believe this is a temporary fix. This feature is best served per-client as a toggleable UI option and this would pair wonderfully with a ping report. This is a fairly common feature across different online games, and would help me and other creators generate better content for users in general. As a preference I'd love to either have this data in the quick menu, or shown above/in conjunction with nameplates.\n\nIf there's anything I can do to help this feature become implemented I'd love to help! Thank you!",
